            "review_text": "lilybt\n6167 contributions\n11\nEast-West Fusion\nAug 2024 • Family\nVietnamese sweetness is a fusion of Chinese and European origin. Located in the northern part of the old town, it's famous for its puddings, but it's a little different from the European creamy ones in that it's like a fine \"pucci-punch\" with a plump texture. When you combine it with coconut milk, tapioca, etc., it is Chinese, and these two vectors mysteriously mesh.\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten July 17, 2025",
