            "review_text": "Henry P\n27 contributions\n0\nSuper cheap, huge variety of Vietnamese desserts\nFeb 2017 • Solo\nI was lost trying to find my hotel when I stumbled upon this place. Traditional Vietnamese desserts (Che) are extremely cheap in Hanoi, generally less than $2. I love desserts, so I tried two. \n\nI had the yogurt jackfruit (VND 22k) and the Green Tea Caramel, which was basically a French creme caramel with a green tea soup, tapioca pearls and some kind of ridged jellies. Of the two, this was my preferred dessert. \n\nThe place was clearly popular among the locals and certainly worth the visit if you're in the area. There was both indoor as well as outdoor seating.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 8, 2017",
